you can call it divine masculinity or any number of things.

1313
01:02:53.270 --> 01:02:55.440
But in this moment right now,

1314
01:02:55.440 --> 01:02:59.250
there's this sense that we need to be embarrassed as men,

1315
01:02:59.250 --> 01:03:01.360
or we're not allowed to be men,

1316
01:03:01.360 --> 01:03:06.360
or it's unclear what the appropriate role is

1317
01:03:06.990 --> 01:03:11.670
for a man because of the culture.

1318
01:03:11.670 --> 01:03:14.430
So we should just sort of step back.

1319
01:03:14.430 --> 01:03:18.140
And it's confusing as somebody who's a father also,

1320
01:03:18.140 --> 01:03:22.323
like, what is the role like, okay provider, protector,

1321
01:03:23.780 --> 01:03:25.950
but I also need to be emotionally available

1322
01:03:25.950 --> 01:03:27.700
and I need to be strong,

1323
01:03:27.700 --> 01:03:28.910
but I also need to be the guy

1324
01:03:28.910 --> 01:03:31.030
who goes to every school event.

1325
01:03:31.030 --> 01:03:35.900
And it becomes like it's much more complicated than it was

1326
01:03:35.900 --> 01:03:39.420
in the era of our parents or my parents

1327
01:03:39.420 --> 01:03:41.850
who are a little bit older than yours,

1328
01:03:41.850 --> 01:03:44.600
where it was little bit more binary

1329
01:03:44.600 --> 01:03:47.200
and that had its problems of course.

1330
01:03:47.200 --> 01:03:48.480
But I find oftentimes,

1331
01:03:48.480 --> 01:03:51.963
like I can't do all of these things all of the time.

1332
01:03:54.030 --> 01:03:55.170
Right?

1333
01:03:55.170 --> 01:03:56.630
Yeah.
It's hard.

1334
01:03:59.835 --> 01:04:03.183
I don't know if it has to be that hard though.

1335
01:04:04.340 --> 01:04:07.263
If you're the way I see it,

1336
01:04:08.710 --> 01:04:13.710
heart-centered, masculine energy leads like your values

1337
01:04:15.920 --> 01:04:20.920
and the direction that you're oriented to

1338
01:04:21.660 --> 01:04:25.030
comes from your ethics, your heart,

1339
01:04:25.030 --> 01:04:30.030
your love for your family, protecting the world,

1340
01:04:30.530 --> 01:04:33.030
protecting people, doing the right thing.

1341
01:04:33.030 --> 01:04:35.430
That's where your direction comes from.

1342
01:04:35.430 --> 01:04:38.510
And then it's all the other parts of you a man,

1343
01:04:38.510 --> 01:04:43.110
I find like the beast in me that helps me go execute

1344
01:04:43.110 --> 01:04:44.620
and go make it so,

1345
01:04:44.620 --> 01:04:47.330
and to protect, yes, I have to,

1346
01:04:47.330 --> 01:04:49.930
I have to learn to be dangerous.

1347
01:04:49.930 --> 01:04:51.310
In fact, like when I didn't,

1348
01:04:51.310 --> 01:04:55.890
when I wasn't in touch with my ability to be destructive

1349
01:04:55.890 --> 01:04:57.840
when I was almost, you know, in many ways,

1350
01:04:57.840 --> 01:05:01.530
emasculated by a sort of a feminist ideology

1351
01:05:01.530 --> 01:05:05.680
where no one like culturally,

1352
01:05:05.680 --> 01:05:08.240
no one wanted me to be dangerous

1353
01:05:08.240 --> 01:05:12.310
so they made me, they emasculated that part of me.

1354
01:05:12.310 --> 01:05:13.720
And then I became more dangerous

1355
01:05:13.720 --> 01:05:16.430
because all of that came out in shadow.

1356
01:05:16.430 --> 01:05:17.263
And I started doing things

1357
01:05:17.263 --> 01:05:19.673
that were subconsciously destructive.

1358
01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:24.490
And I wasn't stepping into that beast part of me

1359
01:05:24.490 --> 01:05:29.490
to actually protect and serve women and my community.

1360
01:05:30.360 --> 01:05:34.200
And so I feel like you have to be in touch with that,

1361
01:05:34.200 --> 01:05:38.253
but like be oriented from the heart space.

1362
01:05:40.690 --> 01:05:44.200
As an actor, that's sort of traditionally conjured as

1363
01:05:44.200 --> 01:05:46.990
a feminine expression, right?

1364
01:05:46.990 --> 01:05:50.420
It's a more feminine energy to be an artist,

1365
01:05:50.420 --> 01:05:51.730
to be a musician.

1366
01:05:51.730 --> 01:05:54.010
Those things would be associated,

1367
01:05:54.010 --> 01:05:56.190
at that end of the spectrum.

1368
01:05:56.190 --> 01:05:57.770
On some level I feel like

1369
01:05:57.770 --> 01:06:00.950
the conversation around divine masculinity

1370
01:06:00.950 --> 01:06:03.030
has an inherent femininity to it

1371
01:06:03.030 --> 01:06:06.640
because you're saying we need to learn how to connect

1372
01:06:06.640 --> 01:06:07.473
with the heart,

1373
01:06:07.473 --> 01:06:10.373
which is not traditionally a masculine attribute.

1374
01:06:11.840 --> 01:06:12.690
We're both.

1375
01:06:12.690 --> 01:06:16.140
Of course we're all, we're an amalgam of these energies.

1376
01:06:16.140 --> 01:06:20.260
So first we have to recognize the inherent femininity

1377
01:06:20.260 --> 01:06:22.660
within all of us as males.

1378
01:06:22.660 --> 01:06:27.660
Yeah I think maybe back in the day,

1379
01:06:27.750 --> 01:06:29.540
if things were more binary and simple

1380
01:06:29.540 --> 01:06:33.890
in which men attempted to be so masculine,

1381
01:06:33.890 --> 01:06:37.210
that it was just like undeniable that you were a man,

1382
01:06:37.210 --> 01:06:38.783
you had to prove it so much

1383
01:06:38.783 --> 01:06:40.770
that you lost touch of the subtlety

1384
01:06:40.770 --> 01:06:43.263
and the dynamic within ourselves.

1385
01:06:45.010 --> 01:06:49.657
But now I find myself to be ready really even leveled,

1386
01:06:52.680 --> 01:06:54.780
still very much in touch with my feminine.

1387
01:06:55.970 --> 01:07:00.830
And yet I've started to cultivate in fashion,

1388
01:07:00.830 --> 01:07:04.140
the more edgier masculine parts of myself

1389
01:07:05.350 --> 01:07:08.250
to really bring myself into balance.

1390
01:07:08.250 --> 01:07:09.280
And what does that look like.

1391
01:07:09.280 --> 01:07:11.457
Like how have you done that?

1392
01:07:12.640 --> 01:07:14.540
Well, I now live on a farm,

1393
01:07:14.540 --> 01:07:17.010
so plenty of-
Hands are in the soil.

1394
01:07:17.010 --> 01:07:18.123
Hands in the soil.

1395
01:07:20.006 --> 01:07:23.160
Using my body and my hands and working my muscles

1396
01:07:23.160 --> 01:07:26.670
and lifting heavy things and building things

1397
01:07:26.670 --> 01:07:31.670
and wanting to protect my kingdom and setting it up

1398
01:07:32.180 --> 01:07:36.713
so that there's a safe space for people to come and be,

1399
01:07:39.690 --> 01:07:40.850
for my family to live in.

1400
01:07:40.850 --> 01:07:41.683
Yeah.

1401
01:07:43.620 --> 01:07:47.700
So much of this in addition to being,

1402
01:07:47.700 --> 01:07:49.763
in this period of time where,

1403
01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:53.190
so many young people grow up without dads,

1404
01:07:53.190 --> 01:07:57.990
we're also in a culture in which we've been

1405
01:07:57.990 --> 01:08:00.730
robbed of traditional rites of passage

1406
01:08:00.730 --> 01:08:04.180
that teach us how to become heart-centered men

1407
01:08:04.180 --> 01:08:05.170
in so many ways.

1408
01:08:05.170 --> 01:08:08.040
And a result,

1409
01:08:08.040 --> 01:08:10.880
it's no surprise that you see these movements out there

1410
01:08:10.880 --> 01:08:13.360
of men congregating trying to recapture

1411
01:08:13.360 --> 01:08:16.860
some aspect of that or to create that for themselves

1412
01:08:16.860 --> 01:08:18.990
later in life in their own lives.

1413
01:08:18.990 --> 01:08:23.050
And I think that that's also why you see all these,

1414
01:08:23.050 --> 01:08:25.770
whether it's Spartan or like all these challenges

1415
01:08:25.770 --> 01:08:27.880
or running a marathon it's because-

1416
01:08:27.880 --> 01:08:28.713
Sports.

1417
01:08:28.713 --> 01:08:31.380
We don't have what we used to have as tribal cultures

1418
01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:33.490
that would put us through the ringer

1419
01:08:33.490 --> 01:08:36.770
and teach us what it means to do something hard.

1420
01:08:36.770 --> 01:08:38.950
And the confidence that comes with that

1421
01:08:38.950 --> 01:08:42.850
and the kind of acceptance that you would receive

1422
01:08:42.850 --> 01:08:47.290
within the tribal community for passing those rights.

1423
01:08:47.290 --> 01:08:49.840
Yeah, absolutely.

1424
01:08:49.840 --> 01:08:54.840
You know, as our culture expands and becomes more spread out

1425
01:08:55.440 --> 01:08:59.630
throughout the world, it's harder and harder to have that,

1426
01:08:59.630 --> 01:09:03.330
that those intimate rites of passage that is,

1427
01:09:03.330 --> 01:09:04.370
are passed down.

1428
01:09:04.370 --> 01:09:07.623
So when we have these sort of,

1429
01:09:09.330 --> 01:09:12.240
placeholder or these alternatives,

1430
01:09:12.240 --> 01:09:14.620
which are standards yeah.

1431
01:09:14.620 --> 01:09:15.870
Stand-ins for,

1432
01:09:15.870 --> 01:09:20.543
for that sports teams and all that kind of stuff.

1433
01:09:21.730 --> 01:09:25.940
I personally have been doing a lot of men's work,

1434
01:09:25.940 --> 01:09:28.190
working with other men

1435
01:09:28.190 --> 01:09:32.413
to bring each other through these rites of passage.

1436
01:09:33.480 --> 01:09:36.340
And it's been so important, so helpful.

1437
01:09:36.340 --> 01:09:37.970
And what are those experiences like,

1438
01:09:37.970 --> 01:09:40.883
like therapeutic or more like tactile?

1439
01:09:42.120 --> 01:09:44.780
Lifesaving just enriching,

1440
01:09:44.780 --> 01:09:49.590
just feel so blessed to have the kinds of men

1441
01:09:49.590 --> 01:09:52.880
that I do in my life too, which I never had.

1442
01:09:52.880 --> 01:09:53.713
You know, I never had brothers.

1443
01:09:53.713 --> 01:09:56.750
I never had those parental role models,

1444
01:09:56.750 --> 01:09:59.030
male parental role models.

1445
01:09:59.030 --> 01:10:02.230
But now I do through my brothers and now I'm an adult.

1446
01:10:02.230 --> 01:10:03.063
I'm a man.

1447
01:10:03.063 --> 01:10:07.760
I now can start to work on being that role model for others,

1448
01:10:08.670 --> 01:10:13.557
but to have other men to model things for me

1449
01:10:13.557 --> 01:10:17.580
and to push against me and to hold me accountable,

1450
01:10:17.580 --> 01:10:20.660
iron sharpens iron so there's a lot of,

1451
01:10:20.660 --> 01:10:23.410
the masculine energy wants to have that pushback

1452
01:10:23.410 --> 01:10:28.310
and that the wrestling or the horseplay

1453
01:10:29.370 --> 01:10:30.980
is so important.

1454
01:10:30.980 --> 01:10:35.980
And then the desire, the philosophical impetus

1455
01:10:38.610 --> 01:10:41.300
to make the world a better place.

1456
01:10:41.300 --> 01:10:44.600
I used to hang out with people who wasn't really interested

1457
01:10:44.600 --> 01:10:45.640
in making the world a better place,

1458
01:10:45.640 --> 01:10:48.010
or just where's the next fix, or

1459
01:10:48.010 --> 01:10:52.880
where's the next good time, a lot of Machiavellian,

1460
01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:53.970
how can I get mine?

1461
01:10:53.970 --> 01:10:56.900
And how can I exploit the situation to make more money,

1462
01:10:56.900 --> 01:10:59.170
or get more fame, or get more things.

1463
01:10:59.170 --> 01:11:01.430
Now, the men that I surround myself with

1464
01:11:02.430 --> 01:11:07.000
want to lead the world into,

1465
01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:12.000
I guess, a better, more stable way of being, yeah.

1466
01:11:12.460 --> 01:11:13.293
It's great, man.

1467
01:11:13.293 --> 01:11:14.126
Yeah it's awesome.

1468
01:11:14.126 --> 01:11:15.770
How do we scale this up?

1469
01:11:15.770 --> 01:11:20.240
Yeah, we've talked about it because it's not fair.

1470
01:11:20.240 --> 01:11:23.590
It's like, how can you be rich if your neighbors,

1471
01:11:23.590 --> 01:11:25.630
you can't be rich unless your neighbors are rich.

1472
01:11:25.630 --> 01:11:28.720
You can't be fully divine masculine

1473
01:11:28.720 --> 01:11:30.594
if your neighbors aren't.

1474
01:11:30.594 --> 01:11:34.623
We have to do this on mass, like at scale.

1475
01:11:36.063 --> 01:11:38.310
And there's not one size fits all,

1476
01:11:38.310 --> 01:11:42.637
but I would encourage everybody to seek groups,

1477
01:11:43.870 --> 01:11:48.463
seek local groups that meet in person to wrestle with this.

1478
01:11:49.690 --> 01:11:52.220
'Cause there's not one formula,

1479
01:11:52.220 --> 01:11:54.077
but it's just showing up.

1480
01:11:54.077 --> 01:11:57.610
And that's the most important lesson that I've learned

1481
01:11:57.610 --> 01:11:59.340
from my men's groups.

1482
01:11:59.340 --> 01:12:02.170
There's not one thing you're supposed to learn

1483
01:12:02.170 --> 01:12:04.083
except just to show up.

1484
01:12:05.257 --> 01:12:09.890
Don't retreat, don't dip because we all,

1485
01:12:09.890 --> 01:12:11.913
all of us in the group have,

1486
01:12:12.960 --> 01:12:14.670
and we've all shared this,

1487
01:12:14.670 --> 01:12:17.200
that we all have imposter syndrome.

1488
01:12:17.200 --> 01:12:20.440
Like, why do I belong here?

1489
01:12:20.440 --> 01:12:22.939
This sense of belonging, like, oh,

1490
01:12:22.939 --> 01:12:24.760
all these men are amazing.

1491
01:12:24.760 --> 01:12:27.900
Who am I to be here with these incredible humans?

1492
01:12:27.900 --> 01:12:29.280
And they all feel the same way,

1493
01:12:29.280 --> 01:12:32.620
and everybody is wrestling with the self-doubt

1494
01:12:32.620 --> 01:12:34.200
or the insecurity.

1495
01:12:34.200 --> 01:12:37.170
And so we just remind ourselves, just keep showing up,

1496
01:12:37.170 --> 01:12:39.580
just keep being vulnerable and keep opening yourself.

1497
01:12:39.580 --> 01:12:41.850
Because when you do it helps the group

1498
01:12:41.850 --> 01:12:43.240
and we help each other.

1499
01:12:43.240 --> 01:12:46.373
So I would just say, do you out there.

1500
01:12:47.760 --> 01:12:52.760
If you are seeking more, you want more from life and from,

1501
01:12:53.360 --> 01:12:56.450
you want to be, you want to improve yourself.

1502
01:12:56.450 --> 01:12:59.010
And as Christian Merde says,

1503
01:12:59.010 --> 01:13:02.660
transform the individual and go find others

1504
01:13:02.660 --> 01:13:03.700
and do that together.

1505
01:13:03.700 --> 01:13:06.710
But all you really have to do is just show up.

1506
01:13:06.710 --> 01:13:08.170
And be honest.

1507
01:13:08.170 --> 01:13:09.287
That's the big piece.

1508
01:13:09.287 --> 01:13:10.720
And I think a lot of men,

1509
01:13:10.720 --> 01:13:14.860
really struggle with the ability to

1510
01:13:14.860 --> 01:13:16.910
summon the courage to be vulnerable,

1511
01:13:16.910 --> 01:13:19.340
especially amongst other men.

1512
01:13:19.340 --> 01:13:21.530
But by creating a safe space

1513
01:13:21.530 --> 01:13:25.220
in order for that to be communicated.

1514
01:13:25.220 --> 01:13:28.620
I think the benefits of that, can't be overstated.

1515
01:13:28.620 --> 01:13:32.650
I mean, this is something I learned immediately in 12 step,

1516
01:13:32.650 --> 01:13:36.400
and I of course get a lot of that out of men's groups

1517
01:13:36.400 --> 01:13:37.670
that I go to in that context.

1518
01:13:37.670 --> 01:13:39.960
But I also have another men's group

1519
01:13:39.960 --> 01:13:41.270
that I meet with once a week.

1520
01:13:41.270 --> 01:13:42.490
And it's like,

1521
01:13:42.490 --> 01:13:46.590
seven guys it's mediated by a therapist,

1522
01:13:46.590 --> 01:13:50.020
been doing it for coming up on three years now.

1523
01:13:50.020 --> 01:13:51.100
Nice.

1524
01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:53.670
And it's just been unbelievable.

1525
01:13:53.670 --> 01:13:55.520
And that's not an addiction based one.

1526
01:13:55.520 --> 01:13:57.780
That's just, we get together.

1527
01:13:57.780 --> 01:13:58.930
Here's what's going on with me.

1528
01:13:58.930 --> 01:14:00.170
What's going on with you.

1529
01:14:00.170 --> 01:14:02.030
We mutually support each other.

1530
01:14:02.030 --> 01:14:05.632
And now we know each other so well, that we can,

1531
01:14:05.632 --> 01:14:07.770
we know everybody's blind spots,

1532
01:14:07.770 --> 01:14:10.897
or we've seen the patterns like you keep doing this thing

1533
01:14:10.897 --> 01:14:12.360
and you say, you're not going to do it

1534
01:14:12.360 --> 01:14:13.560
and then you've done it again.

1535
01:14:13.560 --> 01:14:15.320
Or we give the feedback

1536
01:14:15.320 --> 01:14:17.130
and the person doesn't take the feedback,

1537
01:14:17.130 --> 01:14:18.600
and then we have to deal with the problem

1538
01:14:18.600 --> 01:14:20.310
in the aftermath of it.

1539
01:14:20.310 --> 01:14:22.580
And it's just been amazing, you know?

1540
01:14:22.580 --> 01:14:25.500
And it's something that I think again,

1541
01:14:25.500 --> 01:14:27.860
to like look to camera, like, if you're out there,

1542
01:14:27.860 --> 01:14:30.040
this is something you can do in your own community

1543
01:14:30.040 --> 01:14:31.670
with your friends.

1544
01:14:31.670 --> 01:14:33.840
Maybe you get a therapist involved or somebody else

1545
01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:35.530
who has some level of expertise,

1546
01:14:35.530 --> 01:14:38.020
but if you don't have access to that,

1547
01:14:38.020 --> 01:14:39.770
there's nothing stopping you from getting

1548
01:14:39.770 --> 01:14:42.900
a group of dudes together to just talk in a safe space

1549
01:14:42.900 --> 01:14:44.853
where it's like, this is confidential.

1550
01:14:46.470 --> 01:14:48.510
But the intention is different than like getting together

1551
01:14:48.510 --> 01:14:50.280
with your friends and going out to a bar?

1552
01:14:50.280 --> 01:14:51.113
Of course.

1553
01:14:51.113 --> 01:14:52.340
Or getting with your friends and going out and like,

1554
01:14:52.340 --> 01:14:53.350
you know 4 wheels.

1555
01:14:53.350 --> 01:14:55.160
No, we're not going to watch the game

1556
01:14:55.160 --> 01:14:58.520
and it's not activity based like this is very focused.

1557
01:14:58.520 --> 01:15:00.480
Right, and that is maybe the challenge,

1558
01:15:00.480 --> 01:15:03.240
because we haven't been taught how to do that necessarily.

1559
01:15:03.240 --> 01:15:07.347
So I guess maybe not to oversimplify, it's like,

1560
01:15:07.347 --> 01:15:08.940
oh, just so easy.

1561
01:15:08.940 --> 01:15:10.100
Just go do it.

1562
01:15:10.100 --> 01:15:13.730
But, I guess it's important to just know that

1563
01:15:13.730 --> 01:15:16.340
it's getting together with other men,

1564
01:15:16.340 --> 01:15:21.340
specifically men and sitting in an allotted time

1565
01:15:21.480 --> 01:15:24.477
in a safe space where you communicate vulnerably

1566
01:15:24.477 --> 01:15:27.680
and it's very confidential

1567
01:15:27.680 --> 01:15:30.700
so that you can start to open up

1568
01:15:30.700 --> 01:15:33.410
some of the lower, the deeper layers

1569
01:15:33.410 --> 01:15:36.480
